######################################################################################################################################
# de novo assembly of transcriptomes (RNA-Seq), without needing reference genome 
# First module -> Inchworm: Assembles the reads into longer linear sequences called contigs. It does this by looking for overlaps based on fixed-length words (K-mers).
# Second module -> Chrysalis: Clusters the related contigs and builds De Bruijn graphs for each cluster. Each graph represents the complexity of a gene (or a set of overlapping genes).
# Thirt module -> Butterfly: Processes the graphs and reconstructs the final transcript sequences, separating different alternative splicing isoforms and allelic variants.
######################################################################################################################################
